<SiteLayout title="Security and data handling — Retail POS Mobile" description="Read current security principles and limitations for Retail POS Mobile. Production security claims will be published only when supported by evidence." path="/security/">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Security</div><span class="eyebrow">Trust through evidence</span><h1>Security claims should be earned.</h1><p>Retail POS Mobile is in foundation development. This page records design principles and what remains to be verified before a public release.</p><div class="status-line"><span class="status-pill status-foundation"><span class="status-dot"></span> Foundation stage</span></div></div></section>
<section class="content-section"><div class="container content-wrap"><h2>Architecture principles</h2><div class="content-grid"><article class="content-card"><h3>Independent data boundary</h3><p>The mobile project is designed as an independent product, not a client of another POS database or credential set.</p></article><article class="content-card"><h3>Local and cloud responsibilities</h3><p>The intended architecture separates local device storage, queued operations, and an independent cloud backend.</p></article><article class="content-card"><h3>Server-side authorization</h3><p>Workspace isolation and server-side access control are requirements for the backend; they must be verified in implementation and tests.</p></article><article class="content-card"><h3>No service-role key in the app</h3><p>The project rule is that a Supabase service-role key must never be bundled into the mobile application.</p></article></div>
<h2>What we are not claiming</h2><p>This site does not claim an independent security certification, penetration test, compliance status, production audit, or guarantee of uninterrupted service. Those claims require evidence and a clearly defined scope.</p><h2>What will be published before launch</h2><ul><li>Actual authentication, role, and device-control behavior.</li><li>What data is stored locally and in the cloud.</li><li>How backups, recovery, and synchronization work, if implemented.</li><li>Verified release-signing and update-integrity procedures.</li><li>Known limitations relevant to shop and transaction data.</li></ul><div class="notice"><span class="notice-icon" aria-hidden="true">i</span><div><strong>Current stage</strong><p>The product is not being presented as a public production POS. This page will be updated when implementation and test evidence exists.</p></div></div></div></section></SiteLayout>
